{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For he firmly swore.</b> One oath after another he administered to his brothers, that they would administer to their sons, generation after generation. He said to them: I am not imposing upon you unjustly — Shechem, you stole me, as it is written ״ויבא שכמה״ (and he came to Shechem); to Shechem you must return me. And so they did, as it is written ״ואת עצמות יוסף אשר העלו ממצרים קברו בשכם״ (and the bones of Joseph, which the children of Israel brought up from Egypt, they buried in Shechem)."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:38.617167588Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}